        {
          "id": 1959251269,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Is it time to just have a single CMake flag that accepts a comma-separated list of sanitizer names, so that when the *next* sanitizer is introduced, we don't have to change anything to support it?\n\nSome of the sanitizers seem to require a linker -fsanitize= flag, others don't - or, at least, the CMake files add such a flag for some sanitizers but not others.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-06-20T08:07:43.434Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-20T09:10:49.638Z",
