        {
          "id": 1959296535,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I have no strong opinion on that, but I will say that my CMake skills are still rather minimal -- what I've done here was mostly achieved by following existing patterns -- so I probably wouldn't volunteer to implement the comma-separated list approach just now.  I have no qualms with dropping this MR if the list approach is desired.\n\nI am not presently aware of any more sanitizers we would want to consider supporting.\n\nMy motivation for implementing LSan support is that I've been poking around with fuzzers and ASan and have encountered some issues which have proven difficult to properly debug with ASan active, and it's been somewhat useful to have the option of running with just LSan.  I acknowledge that this is not a common scenario, so I'd even be fine with dropping the MR and keeping it as a local patch if no-one else is likely to ever want to use it. :smile:",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "dariusd0",
            "state": "active",
